(a) The city manager or his/her designee shall provide written notice to an alcoholic beverage handling permit holder of the city manager's or his/her designee's intention to impose one or more of the following administrative penalties:
(1) Suspend their permit;
(2) Revoke their permit;
(3) In addition, impose an administrative monetary penalty as follows: $50.00 for the first offense; $150.00 for a second offense within a 12-month period; an administrative monetary penalty not to exceed $1,000.00 for the third or subsequent offense within a 12-month period; or
(4) Convey a warning for any violation of this division, of O.C.G.A. title 3, or of Subtitle 560-2 of the Georgia Regulations pertaining to the Alcohol and Tobacco Tax Division of the Georgia Department of Revenue.
Such written notification shall set forth in reasonable detail the facts supporting such violation, shall set forth the proposed administrative penalty(ies), and shall notify the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder of their right to appeal under the provisions of this division. Said written notification shall be mailed to the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder at the address set forth in the applicable application, and a copy of said written notification shall be hand delivered to the premises where said violation(s) are alleged to have occurred.
(b) An alcoholic beverage handling permit holder may appeal the proposed administrative penalty(ies) by providing written notification to the city manager within ten calendar days of the date that said written notification was hand delivered to the premises. The written notification shall include the legal and factual basis upon which the applicant's appeal is based.
(c) In the event that the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder does not timely appeal said proposed administrative penalty(ies), then said alcoholic beverage handling permit holder shall be deemed to agree with said proposed administrative penalty(ies). Further, in the event that said proposed administrative penalty(ies) include the imposition of an administrative monetary penalty, said administrative monetary penalty shall be due and owing to the city within five calendar days of the date of hand delivery of the written notification. The failure to timely pay any administrative monetary penalties shall subject the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder to further administrative penalties.
(d) In the event that the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder does timely appeal said proposed administrative penalty(ies), then the city manager shall set an administrative hearing date that shall occur within 30 calendar days of the filing of the appeal request. Notice of said administrative hearing shall be mailed to the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder at the address shown on the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder's application and a copy of said written notice shall be hand delivered to the premises where said violation(s) are alleged to have occurred.
(e) At the administrative hearing, the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder is entitled to be heard and present evidence on his/her behalf. The city manager shall determine whether the proposed administrative penalty(ies) of the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder as set forth in the written notification is justified using a preponderance of the evidence standard.
(f) The city manager shall consider the following factors in determining whether the proposed administrative penalty(ies) of the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder as set forth in the written notification is justified:
(1) Compliance with the criminal history requirements;
(2) The history of and facts relating to previous violations of this chapter;
(3) Non-alcohol related violations of this Code;
(4) Violations of O.C.G.A. title 3 or of Subtitle 560-2 of the Georgia Regulations pertaining to the Alcohol and Tobacco Tax Division of the Georgia Department of Revenue;
(5) Documented efforts at avoiding violations of this chapter, of O.C.G.A. title 3, or of Subtitle 560-2 of the Georgia Regulations pertaining to the Alcohol and Tobacco Tax Division of the Georgia Department of Revenue;
(6) Community involvement; and
(7) Any other objective and relevant facts.
(g) The city manager, after hearing evidence, shall have the authority to confirm or modify the proposed administrative penalty(ies). The city manager shall issue a written decision on the appeal within 30 calendar days of the date of the hearing. All decisions by the city manager shall be mailed to the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder at the address set forth in the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder's application and a copy of said written decision shall be hand delivered to the premises where said violation(s) are alleged to have occurred.
(h) Any alcoholic beverage handling permit holder may appeal the city manager's decision to the city council within ten calendar days of the date that the adverse decision is hand delivered to the premises. Notice of the appeal shall be delivered in writing to the clerk of the city. The written notification shall include the legal and factual basis upon which the applicant's appeal is based.
(i) The city council shall set a hearing date within 30 calendar days of receiving the appeal request. Notice of said hearing shall be mailed to the applicant at the address shown on the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder's application and a copy of said notice shall be hand delivered to the premises where said violation(s) are alleged to have occurred. At the hearing, the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder is entitled to be heard and present evidence on his/her behalf. The city manager or his/her representative may similarly be heard and present evidence in support of the imposition of the administrative penalty(ies). The decision of the city manager shall not be set aside unless the city council finds it to be:
(1) Contrary to law or ordinances;
(2) Unsupported by substantial evidence on the record as a whole; or
(3) Unreasonable.
(j) All decisions of the city council shall be final. The city council shall issue a written decision on the appeal within 30 days of the date of delivery of the hearing. All decisions by the city council shall be in writing and shall be mailed to the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder at the address set forth in the alcoholic beverage handling permit holder's application and a copy of said written decision shall be hand delivered to the premises where said violation(s) are alleged to have occurred.
(Ord. of 9-6-2016(1), § 2)

